# Vulnerabilities the security scan reports but that are accepted for now.
#
# All three are in Spring Framework 6.2.19, the last open-source 6.2 release. Their
# only open-source fix is Spring Framework 7.0.9, which needs Spring Boot 4.
# (6.2.20 has the fix too, but is for Spring Enterprise Support customers only.)
#
# Remove this whole file when the project moves to Spring Boot 4.
# Accepted 2026-11-28. Review by 2027-02-28 if the upgrade has not happened.

# XSLT views. No service has an XSLT view.
CVE-2026-47884

# WebFlux functional endpoints. No service defines one; the gateway uses configured routes.
CVE-2026-47892

# Server-Sent Events. The notification stream uses them. Spring rates this low: it
# needs a signed-in attacker and action by another user, and cannot expose data.
CVE-2026-47890
